    "description": "A silver haired woman, Mildred Norman, calling herself \"Peace Pilgrim,\" walked more than 25,000 miles, from 1953 to 1981, on a personal pilgrimage for peace. She vowed to \"remain a wanderer until mankind has learned the way of peace, walking until given shelter and fasting until given food.\" In the course of her 28-year pilgrimage she touched the hearts, minds, and lives of thousands of individuals all across North America. Her message was both simple and profound: \"This is the way of peace: Overcome evil with good, and falsehood with truth, and hatred with love.\" This hour-long documentary presents an overview of Peace Pilgrim's life and work.",
